    "note": "This composite uses rigidly moved fragments from separate entries, not a deposited walking dimer. 5SYF assembly chains A-14 with A and B-14 with B supply two Taxol-stabilised tubulin dimers 81.5 A apart (Kellogg et al. 2017). 8RHB supplies an AMP-PNP-bound head and docked linker through E334 from an engineered motor-tail fusion; the tail is omitted (Atherton et al. 2025). AMP-PNP stands in for the illustrated ATP and ADP·Pi states, not measured nucleotide timing. 9L7M supplies the nucleotide-free head through T324 from a cysteine-light construct (Makino et al. 2025); 1BG2 supplies the detached ADP head through I325 (Kull et al. 1996). 3KIN B and D, rat KIF5A residues 339-370, supply the neck coil; rat 339 maps to human KIF5B 337 (Kozielski et al. 1997). cycle-model.cif supplies schematic linker backbones (human 335-336, 325-336 or 326-336, native KIF5B sequence): CA spacing is 3.8 A, spans are below 82% of contour, but peptide geometry is distorted. The short poly-Ala stalk is illustrative; distal stalk and cargo are omitted. Bound heads were placed by tubulin superposition. Coil placement is illustrative, guided by rearward coil density in EMD-8546, not fitted to it (Liu et al. 2017). Free-head poses in panels 2-3 are illustrative. This is a one-head-bound ATP-waiting pathway; at high ATP, binding can precede rear-head release (Mickolajczyk et al. 2015). ATP favours linker docking, not an obligatory rigid swing (Rice et al. 1999; Liu et al. 2017). Head 1 passes head 2: about 16.3 nm for the head, 8.2 nm for the dimer (Yildiz et al. 2004)."
  },
